---
import RobotConversation from './RobotConversation.astro';
---
<RobotConversation>
  <Fragment slot="consent">
    <details data-ai-consent>
      <summary>Optional local model</summary>
      <p>I can answer without a model download. You can also try a small local model that picks a passage from the same experience records. It may fail to find a useful passage.</p>
      <p>Enabling it downloads about 204 MB plus runtime files from model hosts. They receive download requests, never your questions. A compatible GPU is required. Files may stay in your browser cache.</p>
      <button type="button" data-enable>Download and enable AI</button>
    </details>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="about">
  <details class="robot-about">
    <summary>About this conversation</summary>
    <p>
      The replies are AI-written using Tim's published experience. Without the optional
      model, local search selects prepared answers. This is not live AI generation.
      The optional model selects exact passages rather than writing new claims.
      Either mode can misunderstand a question or miss context. Ask Tim to confirm
      anything that matters to a hiring or project decision. The reference list names
      the experiences used, without displaying their full records.
    </p>
    <p>
      Searching and answering happen in your browser, up to 12 questions per chat.
      Completed questions and replies are automatically archived for Tim to read.
      No account is needed. This browser keeps the active chat through refreshes.
      Closing the panel or choosing Clear removes that local copy and starts a new
      chat. Tim's archive remains and is never loaded into this conversation.
      Archiving is best effort and may fail if you leave before a request finishes.
      Closing the panel also stops the optional local model.
    </p>
    <p>
      The optional model runs on your device with <a
        href="https://github.com/mlc-ai/web-llm"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">WebLLM</a
      >. Model: <a
        href="https://huggingface.co/mlc-ai/SmolLM2-360M-Instruct-q4f16_1-MLC"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">MLC SmolLM2 360M</a
      >, using f16 or f32 according to GPU support. WebLLM and the <a
        href="https://huggingface.co/HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-360M-Instruct"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">upstream SmolLM2 model</a
      > use Apache 2.0. See publisher pages for license and provenance.
    </p>
  </details>
  </Fragment>
</RobotConversation>

<script>
  import '../../scripts/robot/host';
</script>
